<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Monetary Council to meet, discuss banks.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Monetary Council to meet, discuss banks.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) was due to meet at 1100 local/1300 GMT on Thursday, a Finance Ministry spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The CMN, Brazil's highest monetary policy body, would mull proposals allowing foreign banks to operate in Brazil and changes to rules for foreign investors seeking to buy shares in Brazilian banks, she said.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358</p>
